WEBVTT

00:01.010 --> 00:06.960
Dear Mother, the chairwoman who could have testified that I am Nadja has died.

00:08.090 --> 00:11.080
When I was desperate, Raphael was the one to save me.

00:11.800 --> 00:13.550
"You have wings of hope."

00:14.240 --> 00:17.180
Encouraged by these words, I head for London.

00:26.530 --> 00:27.690
NAAJA

00:26.530 --> 00:27.690
Nadja

00:27.720 --> 00:30.190
kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:27.740 --> 00:30.190
With your eyes

00:30.190 --> 00:31.350
NAAJA

00:30.240 --> 00:31.350
Nadja

00:31.370 --> 00:33.620
nani ga mieru

00:31.370 --> 00:33.620
What do you see?

00:33.840 --> 00:36.730
haruka tooku hikaru

00:33.840 --> 00:36.730
Shining in the far distance,

00:36.880 --> 00:39.020
mirai no tobira

00:36.880 --> 00:39.020
The door to the future,

00:40.160 --> 00:43.570
sagashiteiru

00:40.160 --> 00:43.570
That's what I'm searching for

00:43.570 --> 00:50.780
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:51.490 --> 00:54.900
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:55.000 --> 00:58.260
arasoimo kitto nakunaru

00:55.000 --> 00:58.260
I'm sure there would be no more fighting

00:58.330 --> 01:01.710
kon nani mo tanoshiku naru

00:58.360 --> 01:01.710
It could be so much more fun

01:01.740 --> 01:05.190
sekai wa hiruikedo hitotsune

01:01.740 --> 01:05.190
The world is wide, but it's still one

01:05.560 --> 01:08.920
tabi no owari wa mienai

01:05.560 --> 01:08.920
I can't see the end of the journey

01:08.950 --> 01:12.110
kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:08.950 --> 01:12.110
God is the only one who can possibly know

01:12.280 --> 01:15.930
itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:12.280 --> 01:15.930
To the people who, someday, I will meet again

01:15.930 --> 01:18.080
te wo furinagara

01:15.930 --> 01:18.080
I will go waving

01:18.230 --> 01:24.970
toki ni wa BURUU ni naru himo aru kedo

01:18.230 --> 01:24.970
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:24.970 --> 01:27.710
ushiro mukanai

01:24.970 --> 01:27.710
But I won't look back

01:27.980 --> 01:33.020
yume ga kanau hima de

01:27.980 --> 01:33.020
Until the day my dream comes true

01:33.190 --> 01:36.570
NAAJA kimi no hoho emi wa

01:33.190 --> 01:36.570
Nadja, your smile

01:36.650 --> 01:39.850
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:36.650 --> 01:39.850
Nadja, you give me courage

02:07.200 --> 02:08.290
So, this is London.

02:09.400 --> 02:12.020
It feels so nostalgic.

02:13.470 --> 02:17.420
Alright! Let's search for the person who sent me my mother's dress.

02:26.190 --> 02:30.560
The Lullaby the Piano is Connected To

02:33.030 --> 02:34.320
Let's see...

02:34.990 --> 02:37.130
Post office...post office...

02:38.340 --> 02:39.030
Found it!

02:41.380 --> 02:42.910
Even if you say so...

02:43.550 --> 02:46.540
I remember the postmark for the parcel was from London.

02:46.810 --> 02:51.720
It's not just about the post mark. There are many other post offices in London besides this one.

02:52.140 --> 02:53.380
I see.

02:55.820 --> 02:59.940
To track down a parcel sent such a long time ago...that's absurd!

03:00.310 --> 03:01.330
No record or anything?

03:01.550 --> 03:03.180
They have all been destroyed.

03:04.120 --> 03:05.180
I see.

03:24.800 --> 03:25.840
This is foolish, isn't it?

03:26.360 --> 03:28.410
To search London without any clues.

03:33.720 --> 03:35.200
Where am I?

03:35.620 --> 03:37.720
What should I do? I'm lost!

03:43.940 --> 03:48.800
The last time I was here, I was with the Dandelion Troupe. I should have paid more attention.

04:00.850 --> 04:02.750
The National Museum?

04:10.900 --> 04:11.590
Christian!

04:12.110 --> 04:15.590
If I find Christian, maybe he can give me some advice.

04:18.890 --> 04:19.860
Young lady.

04:23.360 --> 04:25.680
Please do not run within the building.

04:26.720 --> 04:27.440
I'm sorry!

04:30.450 --> 04:32.890
Um...is Christian here?

04:33.530 --> 04:35.810
Ah, Professor Miller's student?

04:35.930 --> 04:36.670
That's right!

04:36.990 --> 04:40.720
Hm, I think he's gone to some exhibition in Egypt...

04:42.770 --> 04:44.370
Then, what about the director?

04:44.770 --> 04:47.480
Today he has a lecture at Cambridge University.

04:47.710 --> 04:48.720
I see...

04:50.520 --> 04:51.630
How cute.

04:52.820 --> 04:54.840
It looks just like a doll.

04:57.460 --> 04:58.840
These aren't toys.

04:59.110 --> 05:00.690
Molded in the shape of Horus' four sons...

05:00.910 --> 05:06.290
Imsety, Hapy, Duamutef, and Quehsenuef, these are canopic jars.

05:06.990 --> 05:08.290
Canopic jars?

05:08.570 --> 05:11.920
Containers used to hold the organs removed during mummification.

05:12.290 --> 05:13.820
M-mummy's organs?

05:15.260 --> 05:15.970
Sorry.

05:22.170 --> 05:23.430
Now that you mention it...

05:24.840 --> 05:28.320
I heard a rumor that Christian is coming back soon.

05:28.860 --> 05:30.930
I'll investigate it for you.

05:32.270 --> 05:33.060
I appreciate it!

05:41.550 --> 05:42.240
It's here.

05:43.200 --> 05:43.870
Christian.

05:45.420 --> 05:46.260
Christian!

05:46.610 --> 05:47.720
Christian isn't here.

05:48.710 --> 05:50.630
He hasn't been here for a while now.

05:50.880 --> 05:51.720
Is that so...

06:08.090 --> 06:09.050
Ah, a letter.

06:10.140 --> 06:11.470
From Christian.

06:11.890 --> 06:12.950
What does it say?

06:13.620 --> 06:14.480
Dear Edna,

06:14.930 --> 06:17.640
Thank you for taking care of my apartment while I am out of town.

06:18.310 --> 06:25.790
Thanks to the help of a girl named Nadja, Professor Harrison's theory has been verified and our excavation in Egypt has been very successful.

06:26.950 --> 06:27.620
Nadja...

06:28.900 --> 06:30.180
It can't be.

06:31.440 --> 06:33.740
Well, I came back here.

06:36.800 --> 06:38.080
What should I do?

06:38.230 --> 06:39.470
Big sis!

06:40.330 --> 06:42.280
Please return our ball!

06:45.980 --> 06:46.850
Here it comes!

06:52.550 --> 06:53.440
Thanks!

06:54.330 --> 06:56.850
Hey, the preparations in the park have begun.

06:57.120 --> 06:57.980
Yeeeesss!

07:00.010 --> 07:04.080
This is the first park I performed at with the Dandelion Troupe.

07:07.210 --> 07:07.730
Now!

07:13.480 --> 07:15.980
Back then, the customers were all delighted.

07:16.820 --> 07:19.390
But the training was pretty harsh, wasn't it?

07:25.630 --> 07:28.960
One-two-three, one-two-three.

07:29.160 --> 07:29.580
Go!

07:31.410 --> 07:32.120
Too slow!

07:34.770 --> 07:40.120
It isn't enough that you have a little skill at dancing, the customers won't be impressed with this.

07:40.540 --> 07:42.860
I-I'm sorry. Please let me try again.

07:43.380 --> 07:45.700
One-two-three...alright, turn around!

07:48.320 --> 07:50.740
What are you doing? Once more.

07:51.360 --> 07:53.700
Sylvie, aren't you being too strict?

07:54.220 --> 07:59.430
Up until now Sylvie has been our only star...until Nadja arrived.

07:59.770 --> 08:01.430
Jealousy, huh?

08:01.480 --> 08:04.390
Sylvie isn't that kind of woman!

08:06.930 --> 08:09.230
No, no. This isn't good at all.

08:11.820 --> 08:15.080
Back then I thought she was scary but...

08:32.510 --> 08:34.410
Nadja, you did well.

08:35.130 --> 08:35.840
Sylvie.

08:39.320 --> 08:41.670
She was happy as if she were the one who succeeded.

08:42.410 --> 08:45.790
That was the first time I felt like I was a part of the troupe.

08:48.260 --> 08:49.620
T-this is...

08:59.000 --> 09:00.580
They still haven't repaired it?

09:01.470 --> 09:02.260
Kennosuke...

09:03.270 --> 09:06.730
Kennosuke...sometimes he scolded me, but he also gave me encouragement.

09:10.450 --> 09:13.810
I...have also lost my mother and father.

09:14.310 --> 09:15.760
So I understand Rita's pain.

09:16.920 --> 09:19.320
Rita was jealous of your brooch...

09:20.030 --> 09:24.330
But she actually may have been jealous of you, because your mother may still be alive somewhere.

09:27.780 --> 09:30.720
Nadja, it would be great if we could find your mother.

09:31.190 --> 09:34.800
We'll always be friends. We'll be sure to find her!

09:35.340 --> 09:36.180
Kennosuke.

09:36.800 --> 09:37.340
Rita.

09:39.220 --> 09:40.280
Thank you!

09:46.770 --> 09:48.820
For the sake of both of them...

09:49.680 --> 09:50.690
I can't feel down.

09:51.880 --> 09:54.790
That's right! This is the place where I first met Harvey.

09:55.360 --> 09:58.840
Harvey can look for clues about my mother.

09:59.680 --> 10:04.720
Sorry, that reporter went after the Black Rose and hasn't returned yet.

10:05.260 --> 10:06.050
Is that so.

10:06.350 --> 10:09.090
Really...where the heck did he go.

10:09.430 --> 10:10.150
Hey, chief.

10:11.330 --> 10:13.360
We are having an editing meeting now, excuse me.

10:26.170 --> 10:27.280
Christian isn't here.

10:27.870 --> 10:28.790
Harvey isn't here, either.

10:29.400 --> 10:30.540
The Dandelion Troupe as well.

10:31.700 --> 10:35.500
The distance to mother...is slowly widening.

10:39.950 --> 10:40.620
Pay attention.

10:59.600 --> 11:01.260
You're in the way, young lady.

11:14.270 --> 11:14.840
John...

11:16.760 --> 11:17.850
John Whittard!

11:45.990 --> 11:46.560
John...

11:49.890 --> 11:52.210
The John I met in Paris...he's holding a concert?

11:55.200 --> 11:56.090
A special seat, please.

11:59.740 --> 12:03.220
If I spend this, I won't be able to buy food.

12:03.840 --> 12:04.560
Young miss.

12:05.770 --> 12:09.620
I'm sorry, but with those clothes...it's a bit...

12:13.940 --> 12:15.270
If it's about a dress, I have one!

13:49.400 --> 13:50.050
Thank you.

13:50.960 --> 13:56.690
For the encore, I would like to play the piece that I like the best right now. Please, lend me your ears.

14:13.280 --> 14:14.760
T...this song.

14:16.090 --> 14:21.820
Above a quiet forest.

14:22.210 --> 14:28.260
A single shining star,

14:29.050 --> 14:35.470
sings a song of love...

14:35.820 --> 14:41.860
The wind blows gently in the pasture.

14:51.000 --> 14:54.330
That's a beautiful lullaby. Where did you learn it?

14:56.550 --> 15:01.390
I don't remember well. But I've known it for a long time.

15:01.740 --> 15:02.360
I see.

15:03.740 --> 15:06.820
Say Nadja, will you teach it to me?

15:07.690 --> 15:08.160
Sure!

15:15.440 --> 15:21.690
I say goodnight, I say goodnight.

15:22.250 --> 15:26.620
To this hand...

15:27.410 --> 15:34.000
My dear child...

16:07.600 --> 16:09.260
You are... Nadja!

16:11.650 --> 16:14.840
It's been so long! How long have you been in London?

16:15.310 --> 16:18.540
Ah! You came to see my concert, didn't you?

16:18.790 --> 16:19.920
More importantly, John.

16:21.180 --> 16:22.290
I have something to ask you.

16:23.030 --> 16:24.000
Something to ask me?

16:27.630 --> 16:28.470
Etoile?

16:29.630 --> 16:32.220
The piece you played as an encore is called "Etoile"?

16:32.590 --> 16:34.460
Yes. It means "star."

16:35.160 --> 16:38.660
A French composer, who died some years ago, composed it.

16:39.450 --> 16:41.570
I have known that song since I was little.

16:42.980 --> 16:45.570
I didn't think it was a famous song...

16:46.170 --> 16:47.990
But...for some reason I know it.

16:48.290 --> 16:49.550
Ah, wait a moment.

16:52.390 --> 16:54.360
Nadja, look at this.

16:56.390 --> 17:00.070
"Written for Nadja. Etoile" is what it says.

17:01.050 --> 17:03.420
Do you think that this is a coincidence?

17:04.110 --> 17:05.870
Nadja, what's wrong?

17:06.290 --> 17:09.570
The name of the composer is Raymond Coli...?

17:10.630 --> 17:11.640
Colville.

17:12.610 --> 17:13.740
Raymond Colville.

17:25.960 --> 17:31.300
This is probably the man who captured your mother's heart during her first ball.

17:31.940 --> 17:32.920
How do you know?

17:33.420 --> 17:38.180
Because there isn't much written about Raymond Colville.

17:38.820 --> 17:42.400
There are a lot of details about everyone else.

17:42.770 --> 17:47.020
There is only one thing written about him: "Man of Fate"

17:48.010 --> 17:49.930
Man of...fate.

17:52.110 --> 17:52.580
Nadja?

17:53.790 --> 17:56.800
It's possible that Raymond Corville is...

17:57.340 --> 17:59.660
My...father.

18:00.530 --> 18:01.340
What did you say?

18:01.880 --> 18:04.500
John, please tell me more about him.

18:05.090 --> 18:09.310
I think asking Mister Watson would be better than asking me.

18:18.100 --> 18:20.030
Mister Watson, it is John Whittard.

18:22.570 --> 18:23.900
What's the matter, John?

18:24.470 --> 18:25.930
Sorry for disturbing you at this hour.

18:26.420 --> 18:29.360
I have brought a lady with me to see you.

18:30.370 --> 18:30.960
A lady?

18:31.340 --> 18:31.730
Yes.

18:41.360 --> 18:45.950
Can you please tell this young lady about a man named Raymond Corville?

18:46.490 --> 18:49.460
I don't mind what you have to say, so please.

18:51.130 --> 18:56.070
We met in some mansion's villa some years ago.

18:57.330 --> 19:00.860
He often played his own music there.

19:01.900 --> 19:06.190
It was a wonderful piece, as if it had come from a disciple of the music from God.

19:07.080 --> 19:12.510
After that, he proposed to a noble's daughter in Vienna and married her.

19:12.710 --> 19:15.300
Could it be that she was from the Preminger House?

19:16.070 --> 19:17.670
Yes, that was the name.

19:18.190 --> 19:20.560
As I remember, the girl's name was...

19:21.400 --> 19:22.170
Colette!

19:23.130 --> 19:24.360
How do you...

19:25.600 --> 19:27.800
She is...my mother!

19:43.840 --> 19:46.610
Etoile...it was dedicated to Nadja.

19:47.000 --> 19:50.240
Then, isn't it a piece that was written for Nadja's sake?

19:50.950 --> 19:56.430
That's right. Their parents were against the marriage so they came to Paris to marry.

19:56.850 --> 20:00.880
And the thing they made for their daughter was this song.

20:04.730 --> 20:07.100
So, it was my father after all.

20:08.510 --> 20:12.040
Ah, that's right. There is a photo with Raymond. Do you want to see it?

20:12.460 --> 20:12.850
Yes.

20:14.950 --> 20:15.470
Here it is.

20:16.500 --> 20:17.660
This is the photo.

20:18.900 --> 20:21.840
The one sitting at the piano is your father.

20:23.740 --> 20:24.770
This is...

20:26.850 --> 20:27.610
This person is...

20:30.010 --> 20:31.170
My father...

20:32.600 --> 20:36.500
Raymond loved your mother from the bottom of his heart.

20:36.920 --> 20:38.800
And I'm sure he loved you too.

20:59.210 --> 21:00.450
I've met my father...

21:06.200 --> 21:08.470
John, I'm very thankful for today.

21:09.360 --> 21:10.990
I'm glad to have helped.

21:11.780 --> 21:16.370
That's right. There is a party that some friends from the university have organized.

21:16.770 --> 21:18.250
Would you like to come?

21:18.820 --> 21:20.960
Is it okay for someone like me to come?

21:21.230 --> 21:22.420
Everyone would be honored!

21:23.090 --> 21:25.730
I, too, would be delighted if you came.

21:26.720 --> 21:30.340
If I brought a cute girl with me, all my friends would be surprised.

21:38.690 --> 21:40.150
The guest of honor has finally arrived.

21:44.440 --> 21:46.440
Thank you, thank you.

21:52.170 --> 21:54.590
Ah, John. It's been a long time.

21:57.130 --> 21:58.040
Francis...

22:00.220 --> 22:01.130
Nadja...

22:14.480 --> 22:17.740
RONDON donyori haretara PARI

22:14.480 --> 22:17.740
Paris is sunnier than London

22:17.910 --> 22:20.930
KARUMEN menyori PAERIYA suki

22:17.910 --> 22:20.930
Carmen likes paella more than pasta

22:21.370 --> 22:27.570
SUPEEDO no jyoou kimagure yasan

22:21.370 --> 22:27.570
The Queen of Spades is a fickle person

22:28.480 --> 22:29.740
kitto

22:28.480 --> 22:29.740
Indeed

22:32.500 --> 22:34.970
nayan datte muda yo

22:32.500 --> 22:34.970
It's no use worrying about it

22:35.020 --> 22:38.630
kesera sera sera sera

22:35.020 --> 22:38.630
Que sera sera, sera sera

22:38.870 --> 22:43.560
ashita nante itsumo naru youni

22:38.870 --> 22:43.560
Tomorrow's going to be whatever it was meant

22:43.660 --> 22:45.020
naru naru

22:43.660 --> 22:45.020
To be, to be

22:45.420 --> 22:50.350
sekai kaeru tobi KONKUURU

22:45.420 --> 22:50.350
The tree frog won.

22:50.850 --> 22:54.800
yuushou shita yo amagaeru

22:50.850 --> 22:54.800
The world frog jumping contest

22:57.980 --> 23:04.130
koneko chan no ashi no urawa

22:57.980 --> 23:04.130
Under the kitten's paw

23:04.600 --> 23:10.720
otentou sama no nioi da ne

23:04.600 --> 23:10.720
Is the scent of the sun, right?

23:13.580 --> 23:16.940
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

23:13.580 --> 23:16.940
Paris is sunnier than London

23:16.990 --> 23:19.950
KARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

23:16.990 --> 23:19.950
Carmen likes paella more than pasta

23:20.500 --> 23:26.920
michikusa shite iru baaijyanai ne

23:20.500 --> 23:26.920
It's not the time to hang around

23:27.760 --> 23:32.270
kitto kitto

23:27.760 --> 23:32.270
Indeed, indeed

23:40.350 --> 23:41.960
Tomorrow's Nadja

23:41.980 --> 23:44.000
How does it feel when you like somebody?

23:45.110 --> 23:46.720
Francis, whom I danced with for the first time.

23:47.610 --> 23:49.480
Keith, who returned my brooch.

23:50.640 --> 23:51.480
The two before me...

23:51.980 --> 23:52.770
I am alone.

23:54.000 --> 23:55.850
I have to decide. I have to find an answer.

23:56.540 --> 23:58.120
Francis? Keith?

23:59.730 --> 24:01.280
I like you!

24:02.590 --> 24:03.410
Tomorrow's Nadja.

24:03.620 --> 24:06.960
Who do I like? The Ultimate Choice!

24:06.200 --> 24:07.800
Now, the door to destiny opens.
